      '- **Intersystem Bonding:** Providing dedicated termination points for telecommunication, cable TV, and satellite dish grounds.',
      '### 4. Branch Circuits & Receptacles',
      '- **Polarity & Ground Continuity:** Testing every accessible outlet with calibrated circuit analyzers to detect open grounds, reversed hot/neutral lines, and false bootleg grounds.',
      '- **GFCI & AFCI Verification:** Testing millisecond trip thresholds on Ground Fault Circuit Interrupters in kitchens, bathrooms, garages, and exteriors, as well as Arc Fault breakers in living areas.',
      '- **Tamper-Resistant Compliance:** Verifying child-safety shutters on receptacles in habitable rooms.',
      '### 5. Life Safety Devices',
      '- **Smoke & Carbon Monoxide Alarms:** Testing interconnected alarms, verifying manufacture dates (detectors expire after 10 years per NFPA 72), and checking battery backups.',
      '## Common Findings in South Florida Homes',
      'During inspections across Boca Raton neighborhoods—from mid-century ranches in Camino Gardens to 1980s homes in Boca Del Mar—our electricians routinely encounter recurring hazards:',
      '1. **Double-Tapped Neutral Conductors:** Multiple neutral wires jammed under a single screw terminal on the panel neutral bus. When one circuit is serviced, loosening the screw interrupts the shared neutral, creating high voltage imbalances that fry appliances.',
      '2. **Ungrounded Two-Prong Outlets:** In older homes built before 1970, ungrounded Romex wiring leaves appliances without a safe fault-current return path.',
